# fixedbugs, defect 151, lane land186, 2026-10-02 (panel 186 R4).
#
# What the layout check owes a misspelling: a record over `SA` with `x`
# written `xx` both misspells a field and leaves one out, and the misspelling
# is what the author fixes, on its own line, before anything about the record
# can be said. The completeness check of the route's first build ran before
# the program's own unit and said *does not name `x`* instead.
#
# FIX: a declared field the dump does not show is a header macro or a
# misspelling, and only the preprocessor knows which, so the record's every
# layout question stands under `#if defined(xx)`; a misspelling switches them
# off, and the field assertion says `ffi_unknown_field` on the line, as lane
# ffi-macro's `fixedbugs-152-a-field-the-header-lacks-*` cases have it.

extern "fixedbugs-151-unions.h"
    record SA
        kind: i32
        i: i32
        xx: i32  #~ ffi_unknown_field

function touch(s: SA) -> i32
    return s.kind

function main()
    print(1)
